              <b>
                01
              </b>

              <strong>
                A new ingredient
              </strong>

              <span>
                It arrives with a story, a launch and a reason to buy. There is always a next one, because the category needs there to be.
              </span>

            </li>
          
            <li>

              <b>
                02
              </b>

              <strong>
                More products
              </strong>

              <span>
                The new one does not replace anything. It is added. Layering, switching and interaction complexity go up with it, and so does the number of decisions you make before breakfast.
              </span>

            </li>
          
            <li>

              <b>
                03
              </b>

              <strong>
                More barrier stress
              </strong>

              <span>
                Excessive, incompatible or frequently-switched routines can leave skin irritated and stressed. Or they simply do not deliver what was promised, which is its own kind of damage.
              </span>

            </li>
          
            <li>

              <b>
                04
              </b>

              <strong>
                A new concern
              </strong>

              <span>
